      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T23:23:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the 2-parent merge commit case above (lines 115-117), id is the synthetic in-memory/on-disk automerge commit (ObjectId automerge \u003d autoMerger.lookupFromGitOrMergeInMemory(...)).\n\nDoes the automerge commit always have a tree containing .git-blame-ignore-revs if it was present in the merge parents, or could a merge conflict on .git-blame-ignore-revs cause it to be missing or fail to read from the automerge tree? If an automerge conflict occurs on that file, getIgnoreIds will gracefully fall back to empty set (since IOException / missing path is caught), but worth verifying if this behaves as expected for merge changes.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "6db1368e5d70cb0213a85a10ce19be30744eff2c",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
